    'Ha Long Bay' => [
        ['A landscape shaped by water and stone', 'Limestone towers rise from the sea in layered silhouettes, with small coves and passages appearing as you move through the bay. Ha Long is a landscape best understood from the water: the same islands can look dramatic beneath clouds and almost delicate in the evening light. Spending time on deck is as much a part of the experience as the stops along the way.'],
        ['Beyond the view from the deck', 'Cave visits reveal another side of the limestone landscape, with chambers and rock formations hidden inside the islands. A kayak or small boat brings the cliffs closer and gives a different sense of their scale. These experiences depend on the cruise route, so choosing a journey is also about choosing how you want to explore.'],
        ['Life on the bay', 'Fishing communities are part of the story of Ha Long. Where a route includes a community visit, it offers context for the boats and everyday activity seen across the water. An overnight stay adds quieter moments: a changing sunset, dinner on board and the first light between the islands.'],
