    'Hoi An' => [
        ['A trading town with many stories', 'Hoi An grew as a trading port, and its old houses, assembly halls and Japanese Covered Bridge reflect the cultures that met here. Behind the yellow façades are courtyards, carved timber and family histories. Walking slowly through the Ancient Town makes those details easier to notice than simply moving from one landmark to the next.'],
        ['From old streets to open countryside', 'The experience changes outside the centre. Small roads lead through rice fields and vegetable gardens towards the coast. Tra Que offers a connection to the herbs and produce used in local cooking, while An Bang brings a relaxed beach setting. This contrast gives Hoi An more variety than its famous evening streets alone suggest.'],
        ['Flavours and evenings by the river', 'Food is a natural way into the town: cao lau noodles and delicate white rose dumplings are local signatures. Workshops and tailoring add another layer of craft and creativity. As daylight fades, lanterns brighten the streets and the riverside becomes a place to wander, pause for dinner and enjoy the atmosphere.'],
