    'Ninh Binh' => [
        ['Vietnam’s countryside, on a remarkable scale', 'In Ninh Binh, steep limestone hills rise directly from fields and waterways. Villages, temples and working farmland sit within the scenery, giving the area a lived-in character as well as dramatic views. It is a place where a quiet country road can be just as memorable as a famous lookout.'],
        ['Trang An, Tam Coc and the view from above', 'Boat journeys at Trang An and Tam Coc bring you close to the water, passing beneath cliffs and through caves. The pace is gentle, with the landscape gradually opening around each bend. Hang Mua offers a contrasting perspective: a steep stair climb leads to views across the surrounding fields, river and limestone peaks.'],
        ['An ancient capital among the hills', 'Hoa Lu connects this landscape to Vietnam’s early history as the site of a former capital. Its temples add a cultural dimension to a visit focused on nature. Around Tam Coc, cycling is another way to experience the countryside, leaving room to stop at a village, observe the fields or simply enjoy the changing light.'],
