    'Phu Quoc' => [
        ['An island with more than beaches', 'Phu Quoc combines long stretches of coast with a green interior and a history tied to fishing and agriculture. Resort life is one part of the island, but pepper cultivation, fish sauce production and fishing communities give it a distinct identity. A visit can move easily between time by the sea and learning about what the island produces.'],
        ['Choose your own coastal rhythm', 'Long Beach is associated with west-coast sunsets, while other stretches of coastline offer different settings for a relaxed day. Boat excursions provide another perspective on the surrounding islands. Some travellers fill their days with activities; others leave the schedule open for a swim, a book and an unhurried meal.'],
        ['A taste of island life', 'Seafood, locally grown pepper and fish sauce connect the island’s food to its livelihoods. Visiting a producer gives familiar ingredients a new story. Phu Quoc works especially well as a change of pace within a longer journey, with time to enjoy the island beyond a single sightseeing stop.'],
