    'Sapa' => [
        ['Terraces beneath the mountains', 'Sapa’s landscape unfolds in steep valleys, cultivated terraces and mountain ridges. The fields change with the farming seasons, so the view is never a fixed postcard. Mist can soften the hills, while clearer moments reveal the scale of the valley below the town and the high peaks beyond.'],
        ['Walking through the Muong Hoa Valley', 'A walk offers a closer connection to the landscape than a viewpoint alone. Paths pass fields, streams and settlements, with routes ranging from shorter outings to more demanding days. A local guide can explain how the land is farmed and introduce the communities and traditions that shape everyday life here.'],
        ['Culture and the high peaks', 'Sapa is home to different ethnic communities, with distinctive textiles, customs and craft traditions. Encounters are most meaningful when there is time for conversation and respect for daily life. Fansipan adds a different experience, with mountain scenery and religious architecture above the valley. Cloud and weather are part of the experience, so each visit can feel different.'],
