    'Hanoi' => [
        ['A capital discovered at street level', 'Hanoi combines busy commercial streets with lakes, temples and quieter courtyards. In the Old Quarter, shopfronts, small cafés and street kitchens share the pavement with everyday city life. The pleasure of exploring is often in these contrasts: stepping from traffic and conversation into a peaceful interior just a few metres away.'],
        ['History woven into the city', 'Hoan Kiem Lake provides a familiar point of orientation, while the Temple of Literature introduces a different side of the capital’s cultural history. Museums and heritage sites offer context for the streets outside. Rather than treating the city as a quick arrival stop, allowing time to walk and look closely reveals how its different layers coexist.'],
        ['A city to taste and return to', 'A bowl of pho, grilled pork with noodles or a small cup of coffee can become a memorable part of a day here. Food stalls and cafés also create opportunities to pause and watch the neighbourhood. Hanoi rewards curiosity: an early walk and an evening outing can give entirely different impressions of the same street.'],
