    'Da Nang' => [
        ['Where the city meets the sea', 'Da Nang has the energy of a growing city alongside a broad coastline. The beach is part of everyday life, with morning exercise, fishing activity and evening walks giving it a local rhythm. My Khe’s open shoreline makes the contrast with the streets behind it especially clear.'],
        ['Headlands, caves and coastal views', 'Son Tra Peninsula brings wooded hills and sea views close to the city. The Marble Mountains offer another change of scene, combining limestone formations, caves and places of worship. These landscapes make Da Nang a varied stop, with opportunities to move between the coast, cultural sites and the city rather than spending every day in the same setting.'],
        ['A base for Central Vietnam', 'Food and cafés are part of the city’s appeal, and the riverside gives evenings a different atmosphere from the beach. Da Nang can also connect with Hoi An and the route towards Hue. That makes it a useful place to combine coastal relaxation with a wider introduction to Central Vietnam’s heritage.'],
