    'Da Lat' => [
        ['A different side of Vietnam', 'Da Lat’s highland setting gives it a character distinct from the tropical coast. Pine-covered hills, gardens and a central lake sit alongside villas, cafés and busy market streets. The atmosphere encourages slower exploration: a walk, a coffee stop and time to notice the landscape around the city.'],
        ['Gardens, farms and the surrounding hills', 'Flowers and farming are part of the area’s identity. Beyond the centre, countryside excursions introduce a landscape of cultivated slopes and green valleys. Coffee experiences can connect a familiar drink to the place it is grown, while walks offer a chance to enjoy the highland scenery at a more personal pace.'],
        ['City character and outdoor experiences', 'Da Lat also has playful architecture and reminders of its history as a hill station. Local markets bring a lively contrast to its quieter lakes and pine forests. It is this mix of city detail and surrounding nature that gives the destination depth, whether your interest is photography, food or simply a change of atmosphere.'],
